WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.772
Module 12 focused on one central idea: trust the data before you trust the result.

00:00:06.772 --> 00:00:14.297
You learned how to audit a dataset, measure missingness, handle duplicates, convert types safely,

00:00:14.297 --> 00:00:23.287
standardize categories, apply domain rules, investigate outliers, and validate the result after cleaning.

00:00:23.287 --> 00:00:30.436
You also used simple EDA to examine categorical and numeric variables and compare groups.

00:00:30.886 --> 00:00:37.508
These skills are foundational because every later analytical method depends on the quality of the input.

00:00:37.508 --> 00:00:42.043
In Module 13, we will build directly on this work.

00:00:42.043 --> 00:00:47.578
We will use descriptive statistics and visualization to study distributions, compare groups,

00:00:47.578 --> 00:00:51.733
and examine relationships more clearly.

00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:58.838
When you move to the next module, keep the same habit: do not calculate a statistic or create a chart until you

00:00:58.838 --> 00:01:02.186
understand what the underlying data represents.
